## What is NOT covered by this licence

Provision prose in this corpus is original drafting except where a provision is
one of the thirty-seven reproduced from the programme's own released Meridian
Financial pack. Where a provision cites an external instrument, the citation is
a reference and the instrument's own terms govern that instrument:

- US statute and regulation (Titles 12, 15, 17 and 31 of the U.S. Code and the
  corresponding CFR parts; 17 CFR 240.17a-4; Federal Register notices) are US
  Government works and are in the public domain under 17 U.S.C. 105.
- NIST publications, including SP 800-53 via usnistgov/oscal-content (CC0), are
  likewise public domain.
- EU legal texts (GDPR, DORA and its RTS, the EU AI Act and the AI Omnibus) are
  reusable under Commission Decision 2011/833/EU, with the source acknowledged.
- California Civil Code Sections 1798.100 et seq. is a public state statute.
- OFAC sanctions list files are US Government works published without terms of
  use. UK OFSI list data is under the Open Government Licence v3.0. EU FSF list
  data must be fetched from webgate.ec.europa.eu under Decision 2011/833/EU and
  NOT from OpenSanctions, whose redistribution is CC BY-NC 4.0 with a
  commercial-licence condition.
- SEC EDGAR material is published as public information that may be copied or
  further distributed without the SEC's permission.
- Anthropic, Claude's Constitution (January 2026), is CC0. FATF typologies and
  SLSA v1.0 are CC BY 4.0. SPDX licence identifiers are CC0. CLDR currency data
  is used under the Unicode Licence v3.
- PCI DSS v4.0.1, the NACHA Operating Rules, ISO/IEC 27001 and 27002, ISO 4217
  code-list files, SWIFT standards documentation, Visa and Mastercard operating
  rules and specifications, the AICPA Trust Services Criteria, the OWASP API
  Top 10 text, and the IBM/Cowlishaw decTest vectors are NOT reproduced in any
  form. Only their identifiers are cited. See docs/SOURCES.md.
- Datasets under CC BY-NC, CC BY-SA, CC BY-ND, ODbL, a competition-terms clause,
  or a gated agreement are cited and never included — this includes Elliptic,
  IEEE-CIS, COMPAS, the ULB credit-card fraud dataset, IBM AMLworld, and the
  Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac loan performance datasets.
- FRED (Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis) is excluded entirely: its terms of
  use forbid use of the data in machine-learning training.
- Thirty-seven provisions are reproduced from the programme's own released
  Meridian Financial pack, with their text and absolute flags unchanged.
